cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please also credit pyTENAX, from which the SMEV
  estimator in smev.py is derived (see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md).
title: >-
  Extreme areal precipitation across spatial and temporal scales: SMEV return levels, precipitation event spatial organization, and temperature scaling  
abstract: >-
  Python scripts for the analysis of extreme areal precipitation in gridded precipitation and temperature datasets. Mean areal precipitation is computed over moving windows of ws x ws grid cells, yielding a range of spatial scales from the native grid cell to hundreds of kilometres. At each spatial scale, independent ordinary events are extracted across multiple durations, and the Simplified Metastatistical Extreme Value (SMEV) model is fitted to their left-censored upper tail, giving return levels for multiple durations and return periods, with optional year-block bootstrap confidence intervals. Then the workflow characterizes the spatial organization of the underlying precipitation ordinary events (storm footprint area and concentration), and estimates the scaling of event intensity with pre-event temperature by quantile regression, across the same durations and spatial scales.
type: software
